+        // bork: consume ONLY the events we actually acted on. These two calls
+        // used to sit outside `if (doScroll)`, so an overflowing scrollbox ate
+        // EVERY wheel event — including the ones the _prevMouseScrolls axis
+        // filter above deliberately declined, which on a trackpad is most of
+        // them. preventDefault makes EventStateManager::PostHandleEvent take
+        // the eConsumeNoDefault branch and skip the whole wheel default-action
+        // path (scroll target, wheel transaction, APZ handoff), so the live
+        // wheel transaction stayed latched to the tab strip and page scrolling
+        // died for ~25s until it timed out. Same defect that made row 2
+        // unusable; row 2 escaped by dropping the widget, the tab strip
+        // cannot. See scrollback-error.md.
+        event.stopPropagation();
+        event.preventDefault();
+      }
